Text:
fearlessManager is a program. When it starts it attempts to become the 'single' manager.
The 'single' manager applies the messages that fearlessMessage sends, one at a time.
The 'manager path' is the OS path of the ManagerFolder on the actual file system.
projects.info is a file containing an Info serialized as defined in the fearless standard library.
We expect that only the manager can edit this file.
The Info of projects.info is a ProjectsInfo.

Grammar:
ManagerFolder ::= LockFile, "projects.info", "icons", "locks"
//icons and locks are folders.
LockFile ::= "no_manager.lock" | "candidate_manager.lock" | "single_manager_at_", Port, ".lock"
//the syntax of LockFile defines a file name.
Port ::= [1-9][0-9]*//the digits are a port of the loopback address
ProjectsInfo ::= Infos.map("projects", Projects, "reserve", Extensions)
Projects ::= Infos.list(Project1 .. Projectn) //using .list/.map loosely: assuming any arity is allowed
Extensions ::= Infos.list(Extension1 .. Extensionn) //1..n can be empty, Infos.list() == Info
TypeNames ::= Infos.list(TypeName1 .. TypeNamen)
Project ::= Infos.map("path", TaggedText, "kind", Kind, "mains", TypeNames, "mounts", Mount, "attenuators", Attenuator)
Mount ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, ProjectName1 .. TypeNamen, ProjectNamen)
Attenuator ::= Infos.map(TypeName1, TypeNames1 .. TypeNamen, TypeNamesn)
Kind ::= "idle" | "code" | "dataRead" | "dataEdit"
Extension ::= OSExtension
ProjectName ::= ValidSegment
TaggedText ::= \
  "\"" Base16 "\""                      \
  | "\"Str:"  [0-9A-Za-z_.....] "\""     \//complete the .... with fearless Str - \n
  | "\"UStr:" [0-9A-Za-z_.....], "\""
ProgressLine ::= implementation dependent progress information cap to 80 chars.

Well formedness:
in Port: the digits form a number smaller than 65536.
in Extension: not in "fearless" or "ffile000"-"ffile999" or "fapp000"-"fapp999".
in Projects: no two Project with equal TaggedText.
in Extensions: all Extension are disjoint.
in Project: all TypeName in TypeNames are disjoint.
in TaggedText: starts with "\"Str:" if the third component is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless Str encoding a valid OS FS path.
in TaggedText: starts with "\"UStr:" if the third component is the result of\
  p.escape where p is a Fearless UStr encoding a valid OS FS path.

Text:
//add Examples of valid Str and UStr for non trivial cases, where \n and other special symbols are involved.

Invariant:
At every moment, at most one fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.

Story:
A fearlessManager starts.
B No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder with files: \
  empty no_manager.lock,\
  projects.info holding Infos.map("projects", Infos.list(), "reserve", Infos.list()),\
  and the empty folders icons and locks.
D fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
E fearlessManager.serve()

Story:
A fearlessManager starts.
B No folder is at the 'manager path'.
C Another process creates a folder at the 'manager path' before fearlessManager\
  creates the ManagerFolder.
D fearlessManager ends.

Story:
A fearlessManager starts.
B The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile called no_manager.lock,\
  and no process holds the lock of no_manager.lock.
C fearlessManager takes the lock of no_manager.lock.
D fearlessManager.serve()

Story:
A fearlessManager starts.
B The folder at the 'manager path' holds one LockFile called candidate_manager.lock\
  or single_manager_at_X.lock, and no process holds the lock of that LockFile.
C fearlessManager takes the lock of that LockFile.
D fearlessManager renames that LockFile to no_manager.lock.
E fearlessManager.serve()

Story:
A Another process holds the lock of the LockFile of the folder at the 'manager path'.
B fearlessManager ends.

Story:
A The folder at the 'manager path' holds no LockFile, or more than one LockFile.
B fearlessManager.fatalError('manager path', "the folder is not a ManagerFolder")

Define fearlessManager.serve():
A fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the\
  'manager path' is a ManagerFolder.
B fearlessManager renames no_manager.lock to candidate_manager.lock.
C fearlessManager copies base.IconsConflict and base.IconsFearless into icons.
D For each Project of projects.info with the Kind code: Coordinator.dropUnfinished(Project."path").//is this correct?
E fearlessManager.buildMap()
F fearlessManager listens for connections on the loopback address,\
  on a port X that the OS picks.
G fearlessManager renames candidate_manager.lock to single_manager_at_X.lock.
H fearlessManager is the 'single' manager.
I fearlessManager shows its tray icon.
J For each Message arriving on port X, one at a time, in the order the messages arrive: fearlessManager.receive(Message).//confirm Message is in a grammar somewhere.

Define fearlessManager.serve():
A fearlessManager holds the lock of no_manager.lock, and the folder at the\
  'manager path' is not a ManagerFolder.
B fearlessManager.fatalError('manager path', "the folder is not a ManagerFolder")

Define fearlessManager.receive(Message):
A fearlessManager.nameInference()//why this step?
B Message is about Project, Project is registered in projects.info
C fearlessManager.autoCheck(Project)//or Project.Path?
D fearlessManager.apply(Message)

Define fearlessManager.accept(Message):
A fearlessManager sends "Applied" -> Message.connection
B fearlessManager sends "Applied"+Message."what part of it?" -> managerGUI?.connection
C fearlessManager.apply(Message) -> Message.connection //output of running Message is sent
D fearlessManager ends Message.connection
//above managerGUI?.connection is an 'trash all' connection if managerGUI? == empty

Define fearlessManager.refuse(Message, RefusedError):
A fearlessManager sends "Refused"+RefusedError -> Message.connection
B fearlessManager sends "Refused"+RefusedError+Message."what part of it?" -> managerGUI?.connection
C fearlessManager ends Message.connection

Define fearlessManager.apply(Show):
A managerGUI? = ManagerGui.startIfEmpty(managerGUI?) //else identity
B fearlessManager.accept(Show)

Define fearlessManager.apply(Quit):
A fearlessManager sends "Applied" -> Quit.connection
B fearlessManager renames single_manager_at_X.lock to no_manager.lock
C fearlessManager stops listening to X.
D For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager.terminate(p).//async calls
E fearlessManager sends an up to date ProgressLine -> Quit.connection\
  every 2 seconds, until fearlessManager ends.
F all projects are fully terminated
G fearlessManager ends.

Define fearlessManager.apply(Reset):
A fearlessManager sends "Applied" -> Reset.connection
B fearlessManager.reset()

Define fearlessManager.fatalError(FatalError):
A fearlessManager shows FatalError.dialog(busyProjects.names).
B The user closes the dialog.
C fearlessManager.reset()

Define fearlessManager.reset():
A fearlessManager renames single_manager_at_X.lock to no_manager.lock
B fearlessManager stops listening to X.
C For each p in busyProjects: fearlessManager.terminate(p).//async calls
D all projects are fully terminated
E Reconciliator.eradicateAll
F fearlessManager deletes the folder at the 'manager path'.
G fearlessManager ends.

Implementation notes:
The 'manager path' is the folder fearless<version> next to the program folder, the folder holding fearlessManager, fearlessMessage and fearlessOnClick.
fearlessManager creates the ManagerFolder by filling a new folder next to the 'manager path', then renaming that new folder to the 'manager path': the rename fails when a folder is at the 'manager path' already.
The lock of a LockFile is the lock of FileChannel.tryLock: the OS releases the lock when the process ends, however the process ends, and the lock follows the file when the file is renamed.
